{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792102225,"nonce":"3u6Ba84QE5GWMggLvvzIXvyuAvA=","title":"Cache the disabled color-debug probe instead of reading the environment on every lookup","message":"With ASHUI_DEBUG_COLOR_TOKEN unset, ThemeState.color calls debugColor, which calls Sys.getEnv on every lookup while debugSeen stays null. Repeated environment reads allocate in a normal rendered frame even though debugging is disabled.\n\nExact reproducer lives in sibling ChimpMonk: repro/ashui_theme_color_alloc/Repro.hx and repro.hxml. After building the editor once to populate editor/bin native libraries, run from that repro directory: BLINC_CSS=/Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/blinc_abi/target/release/blinc-css haxe repro.hxml; then /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/ash/target/release/ash --preset application ../../editor/bin/ashui-theme-color.hl. The helper uses five allocation windows after warmup and subtracts the GC-stat reading cost.\n\nObserved 8192 calls on local Ash release: theme.color = 262064 bytes; Sys.getEnv alone = 262144; direct colors().primary.rgb() = 0. The source explains the difference: debugColor checks Sys.getEnv every time when tracing is disabled. This is evidence for caching the debug setting in AshUI, not yet evidence of incorrect compiler allocation elimination. A runtime improvement to constant environment-key marshalling could be investigated separately.\n\nA six-round interleaved 500000-call A/B on this loaded host measured best 2.08 ns for assigning the former constant wireframe selection color and 231.04 ns for assigning the token lookup. Load averages were 8.94, 10.91, 10.60. ChimpMonk now caches its selected collider color by theme identity/revision instead of adding this repeated lookup to its render path.\n\nSuggested outcome: read or configure the disabled debug flag once, retain existing theme overrides and trace output, and require zero steady allocation from normal ThemeState.color lookups. No AshUI source changes made for this issue.","files":null}]}